  "recordedBy": "PFD flattener-geometry lane, 2026-09-10",
  "measuredWith": "scripts/rcap-official-forms/scan-inverted-widget-rects.mjs",
  "whatThisIs": "A bounded measurement of ONE demonstrated defect: widgets whose /Rect stores its corners in the inverted order, which ISO 32000-1 7.9.5 permits and requires a consumer to normalise, and which pdf-lib's PDFForm.flatten() places one box away from the control the form draws.",
  "whatThisIsNot": "Not a national source audit, not a freshness review, and not a verdict on any family. It counts one thing and says how it was counted.",
  "howSourcesWereResolved": "By content digest against custody, never by filename. private/ is a mounted custody symlinked into the worktree and the walk follows symlinks; a walk that does not follow it reports an empty custody and proves nothing.",
  "twoScopesAndWhy": "The RECEIPT scope is every source a family's source-receipt.json binds by digest -- the set the builders actually open. The CUSTODY scope is every held AcroForm PDF, bound or not, because a form held but not yet bound carries the same defect the day a family binds it. Reporting only the bound set would understate the population and call it the answer.",
