  "whatTheNumbersMean": "46 inverted-rect widgets in 13 held AcroForm forms, out of 13,023 widgets in 245 forms. Exactly ONE paints today -- Alabama CR-65's Check Box10.2, whose unticked white fill was gouging the word 'expired' out of a statutory eligibility ground on eight families' petitions. The other 45 are empty text fields and unticked boxes whose /N carries no painting operator; each becomes visible the day its family writes it, because pdf-lib regenerates a written field's appearance and flatten places the regenerated stream from the same raw corner. Every one of the 46 is y-inverted; none is x-inverted; offsets run 9.84 to 17.28pt.",
  "correctionsToTheBriefThatCommissionedThis": [
    "The brief described two known instances in 229 widgets and called the population rare. Measured across held custody it is 46 in 13,023. Rare per widget, but present in 13 of 245 forms.",
    "The brief named WV SCA-C907 as the second instance. It is confirmed (MulitipleFelonlySatisfiesDate, |dy| 17.28pt, no painting operator) but it is NOT bound by any family source-receipt today, so a receipt-scoped scan alone would have missed it. WV SCA-C906 carries two more the brief did not name.",
    "Indiana CCA-XP-0220-7010 carries six and IS bound today, by in_conviction_felony-set. That family is held by another lane and was not touched here."
  ],
  "whatWasRepairedHere": [
    "al-pardoned-felony-set",
    "al-felony-nonconviction-90-set"
